.TH PNEUD 1 "2026-10-30" "Pneu" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pneud \- direct file and clipboard sharing between paired devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pneud
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pneu connects paired Android phones and computers over authenticated, encrypted
connections. The Linux desktop integration supports Plasma 6 on Wayland.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the per-user daemon and tray. Normally managed by the systemd user service.
.TP
.B window
Open the desktop window, starting the systemd user service if necessary.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon status.
.TP
.BI "send [--to " "DEVICE" "] " "FILE..."
Send files to eligible paired devices, or to the explicitly selected device.
.TP
.B pair
Create an invitation and print its link and terminal QR code.
.TP
.B join
Read a computer pairing invitation from standard input.
.TP
.B reload
Apply configuration changes supported without a daemon restart.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the complete command list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pneu/config.toml
Configuration, unless XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pneu
Private trust, receipts and queue state, unless XDG_DATA_HOME is set.
.SH NOTES
Clipboard integration requires a Wayland compositor implementing data-control.
A user service installed under ~/.config/systemd/user takes precedence over the
system package's service. Uninstalling preserves user data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
